fficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=19 \\\\ 12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=18.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}-3\\cdot 2=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-6{x}_{1}+(-3)=-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186366602 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366602 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366602 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366602 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366602 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366602 #edb/ref 1076 #