xt{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186394990 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "afea1de7-9432-5f54-8eea-c94a31190309" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394990 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} & -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ 9{x}_{2} &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5\\cdot 1 & =4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186394991 